    <values><field>LongDescription__c</field><value xsi:type="xsd:string">Finds: PriceAdjustmentTier records on the same schedule with overlapping LowerBound/UpperBound ranges.
Why it matters: Overlapping tiers cause nondeterministic pricing — the same quantity gets different adjustments on different runs. ARM picks one tier inconsistently.
Suppress a finding: when overlaps are intentional and a tiebreaker exists elsewhere.
Disable the detector: most ARM orgs should leave this on.</value></values>
